# Every source file in this pack is written LF. Without this, a clone on
# Windows checks out CRLF and the next commit shows every line of every file
# as changed -- which would bury real diffs in a pack whose whole value is
# being able to see what changed between renders.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images and video the docs might carry.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary

# ...except the doc images, which MUST be LFS. The note below says the Hub
# refuses a plain blob over 10 MB; that is out of date. On 2026-08-30 it
# rejected the whole push over three PNGs of 262-545 KB -- "Your push was
# rejected because it contains binary files" -- so the Hub now wants every
# binary in Xet/LFS regardless of size. GitHub's LFS quota is 1 GB and these
# are about 1.1 MB total, so paying it here costs nothing and is what keeps a
# single `git push origin main` reaching both hosts.
docs/img/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

